## Propagating Trace Context Through RabbitMQ Headers

The key is to inject the current `Activity` context into message headers on publish, then extract and restore it on consume.

**Publisher (Service A):**

```csharp
using System.Diagnostics;
using OpenTelemetry;
using OpenTelemetry.Context.Propagation;
using RabbitMQ.Client;

// Create an ActivitySource for your producer
private static readonly ActivitySource Source = new("ServiceA.Publisher");
private static readonly TextMapPropagator Propagator = Propagators.DefaultTextMapPropagator;

public void PublishOrder(OrderEvent order, IModel channel)
{
    using var activity = Source.StartActivity("order.publish", ActivityKind.Producer);

    var props = channel.CreateBasicProperties();
    props.Headers ??= new Dictionary<string, object>();

    // Inject trace context into message headers
    Propagator.Inject(
        new PropagationContext(activity.Context, Baggage.Current),
        props.Headers,
        (headers, key, value) => headers[key] = value);

    channel.BasicPublish("orders-exchange", "order.created",
        basicProperties: props,
        body: Serialize(order));
}
```

**Consumer (Service B):**

```csharp
private static readonly ActivitySource Source = new("ServiceB.Consumer");
private static readonly TextMapPropagator Propagator = Propagators.DefaultTextMapPropagator;

public void HandleMessage(BasicDeliverEventArgs ea)
{
    // Extract context from headers
    var parentContext = Propagator.Extract(
        default,
        ea.BasicProperties.Headers,
        (headers, key) =>
        {
            if (headers != null && headers.TryGetValue(key, out var val))
            {
                // RabbitMQ stores header values as byte[]
                return new[] { val is byte[] bytes ? Encoding.UTF8.GetString(bytes) : val.ToString() };
            }
            return Enumerable.Empty<string>();
        });

    Baggage.Current = parentContext.Baggage;

    // Start a linked activity with the extracted parent
    using var activity = Source.StartActivity(
        "order.process",
        ActivityKind.Consumer,
        parentContext.ActivityContext);

    // Process the message — all downstream spans are now parented correctly
    ProcessOrder(ea.Body);
}
```

**OTel registration (both services):**

```csharp
builder.Services.AddOpenTelemetry()
    .WithTracing(t => t
        .AddSource("ServiceA.Publisher")   // or ServiceB.Consumer
        .AddAspNetCoreInstrumentation()
        .AddOtlpExporter());
```

**Why this works:** W3C `traceparent`/`tracestate` headers get serialized into the RabbitMQ message properties. The consumer reconstructs the parent context, so its spans share the same `TraceId` — giving you a single end-to-end trace in Jaeger/Zipkin/etc.
